  "profile": {
    "name": "Ahmed Soliman",
    "title": "PhD Researcher | Computational Architect & Structural Designer",
    "image": "/assets/xmain.webp",
    "bio": "Ahmed Soliman is a PhD researcher in Architectural Engineering at Vrije Universiteit Brussel, specializing in innovative structures and computational design. His research focuses on deployable scissor structures and rigid plate systems, integrating structural engineering with parametric and computational design approaches. He holds a Master of Science degree from Vrije Universiteit Brussel (VUB) and Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB). With a strong academic and teaching background across multiple universities, he has developed expertise in digital design workflows, sustainability, and advanced fabrication thinking. His work bridges architecture and engineering, driven by a problem-solving mindset and a passion for innovation in construction systems."
